# UI, theme, localization and responsive layout

## Tokens only
- Colors come from AppColors, spacing from AppSpacing, radii from AppRadius, text styles from AppTypography, shadows from AppShadows and icon sizes from AppIconSizes. Read them through the BuildContext extensions.
- Raw Color values and the Colors class are allowed only in lib/core/theme (Colors.transparent excepted).
- No raw font sizes and no numeric literals in EdgeInsets or SizedBox in presentation code. Multiply spacing tokens by LayoutMetrics.scale when a layout must grow with the screen.
- The font family is a single token (AppTypography.fontFamily) backed by bundled Outfit assets. Never fetch fonts at runtime.

## Strings
- Every user-facing string lives in lib/l10n/app_en.arb and lib/l10n/app_my.arb with identical keys. Use ICU plurals for counts.
- Read strings with context.l10n. Never pass a string literal to Text, SnackBar or a tooltip.
- Seed data (product names, section titles) is data, not UI text, and stays in assets/seed.
- AppFailure messages are localized only through the failure localization extension.

## Responsive
- ScreenClass (compact, regular, expanded) comes from width thresholds in LayoutBreakpoints. LayoutMetrics exposes scale, gutter, maxContentWidth, heroImageExtent, isShortHeight and motionScale.
- Layouts use Expanded, Flexible, Wrap and LayoutBuilder. Never wrap text in fixed heights.
- Never clamp the system text scale. Every screen must survive text scale 1.3 on the reference devices in test/helpers/device_matrix.dart.
- Portrait only, locked in Dart and in native configuration.

## States
- Every screen and section has loading, data, empty and failure states rendered through ViewStateBuilder.
- Loading uses skeletons inside a SkeletonScope, never spinners for content.
- Failure views offer retry unless the failure is NotFoundFailure.
- The offline banner is mounted once in the app shell; screens never show their own.

## Widgets
- AppButton handles loading and the double-tap guard. AppTextField is the only text input.
- Keep build methods short: extract private widgets into the screen's widgets folder instead of helper methods returning widgets.
